dd enemies. Risky but visible.\n\nAlternative: change enemy_low[11] to 0x00 -> pointer $9F00 = one byte before the list. $9F00 = byte before is part of the previous area's data. Record bytes: $9F00=0x2B? Wait, $9F00 = ? The list starts at $9F01 with 0x1E. So $9F00 is the byte before, probably the terminator 0xFF of the previous area's list. So pointer $9F00 → first record byte0=0xFF → immediate end of list → NO enemies at all! That's the cleanest, most dramatic proof: repoint 1-1's enemy list one byte earlier (to a 0xFF terminator) and NO enemies spawn.\n\nWait, is $9F00 = 0xFF? Let me check. The note said \"the list begins byte0=$1E and ends with the $FF terminator at prgRom 0x1F1E\". That's 1-1's list end. The previous area's list presumably ends right before $9F01 with 0xFF. Let me read $9EF0-$9F05 to confirm.\n\nActually, changing low byte from 0x01 to 0x00 gives $9F00. If $9F00 is 0xFF (end marker) or some byte with low nibble 0x0F... Actually the spawner's check at $C14B compares byte0 with $FF. If $9F00=0xFF, the spawner immediately ends → no enemies. \n\nBut wait: our layout proof used the value $9F01 and the note says 1-1's enemy list. Let me verify $9F00.\n\nLet me read cpu 0x9EF8 length 12.\n\nActually, even simpler: I could change enemy_low[11] from 0x01 to 0xFF? Then pointer $9FFF, garbage. No.\n\nLet me read $9EF0-$9F02 to see what's there. Then decide.\n\nActually, I realize the cleanest proof would be to point at a *different valid enemy list* and see different enemies, OR to point at the terminator and see none. Both prove the table controls the enemy start. The \"none\" proof is very robust: if I set 1-1's enemy pointer to a byte that is $FF, the spawner stops immediately and no enemies appear. But to make sure $9F00 is $FF, read it.\n\nHmm, but actually there's a subtlety: does the spawner start reading at $E9 (=pointer)? The pointer is $E9/$EA, set from enemy_low/high. If pointer = $9F00 and $9F00=0xFF, spawner sees $FF and ends → zero enemies. Good.\n\nLet me read $9EF0..$9F02.\n\nAlso let me now do a fresh baseline for the enemy proof: the current game is still running the modified layout (from the layout edit) even though we undid the ROM. I need to reset to get back to clean 1-1. Actually reset will use the restored ROM. Good.\n\nPlan for enemy proof:\n1. read cpu $9EF0 length 0x12 to confirm $9F00/$9F01.\n2. write_memory prgRom 7407 = 0x00 (from 0x01), reason.\n3. reset, start 1-1, hold right ~150, screenshot → expect no Goombas (and note baseline had a Goomba).\n4. undo_edit.\n\nActually, the baseline 1-1 screenshot (before layout edit) had a Goomba visible near the hill. With no enemies, that Goomba (and any others) would be absent. That's a clear visual proof.\n\nBut careful: the enemy list is read progressively as the player advances; at the start only the first Goomba is spawned. So the screenshot comparison: baseline showed a Goomba at ~x118; modified should show none.\n\nLet me confirm $9F00. Let me read now (paused? currently RUNNING, but reads fine).\n\nLet me batch: read cpu 0x9EF0 length 18.\n\nAlso, let me get the current baseline Goomba evidence more concretely — the baseline screenshot did show a brown Goomba near the hill at (118,185). Good.\n\nLet me do the read."}
