e pointer detail. Let me keep the level notes focused.\n\nTable note(s):\nid: \"area-layout-pointer-table\"\nname: \"Area layout-data pointer table (low/high by area)\"\nnotes: \"Low bytes at prgRom 0x1D2C (CPU $9D2C) and high bytes at 0x1D4E (CPU $9D4E), 34 entries each; base offsets at 0x1D28 (CPU $9D28), 4 entries indexed by area type $074E. Level-init routine CPU $9C22 ($9C43-$9C56) does LDY $074E / LDA $9D28,Y / CLC / ADC $074F / TAY / LDA $9D2C,Y -> $E7 / LDA $9D4E,Y -> $E8, so the pair is the layout data address (2-byte header; records at +2). World 1-1: $074E=1, $074F=5 -> index 8 -> low 0x8E + high 0xA6 = $A68E (records $A690). PROOF (trace + ledgered write): read trace over 0x1CE0-0x1D6F during a 1-1 reload returned PC $9C49 reading $9D29=3, PC $9C51 reading $9D34=0x8E, PC $9C56 reading $9D56=0xA6; ledgered write prgRom 0x1D34 0x8E->0xF3 made 1-1 load the adjacent area at $A6F3, confirmed by a screenshot showing a different level (tall green-topped pipe platforms) and live $E7/$E8=$A6F5; undone.\"\n\nid: \"area-enemy-pointer-table\"\nname: \"Area enemy-data pointer table (low/high by area)\"\nnotes: \"Low bytes at prgRom 0x1CE4 (CPU $9CE4) and high bytes at 0x1D06 (CPU $9D06), 34 entries each; base offsets at 0x1CE0 (CPU $9CE0), 4 entries indexed by area type (Y from CPU $9C09($0750)). Routine CPU $9C22 ($9C31-$9C41): LDA $9CE0,Y / CLC / ADC $074F / TAY / LDA $9CE4,Y -> $E9 / LDA $9D06,Y -> $EA. World 1-1: base[1]=6 + $074F=5 = index 11 -> low 0x01 + high 0x9F = $9F01. PROOF (trace + ledgered write): read trace over 0x1CE0-0x1D6F during a 1-1 reload returned PC $9C34 reading $9CE1=6, PC $9C3C reading $9CEF=1, PC $9C41 reading $9D11=0x9F; ledgered write prgRom 0x1CEF 0x01->0x00 pointed 1-1 at the $FF end-marker at $9F00, and the Goomba that is present in the baseline run disappeared (list_sprites had only Mario + HUD coin vs a 6-tile palette-7 Goomba), live $E9/$EA=$9F00; undone.\"\n\nAlso maybe a general note id \"1-1-area-data-pointer-tables\" combining. 